                                                                                                                                               "typeName":  "dsDescriptionValue",
                                                                                                                                               "multiple":  false,
                                                                                                                                               "typeClass":  "primitive",
                                                                                                                                               "value":  "This dataset contains data collected during the agricultural season 2020. The experimentation was conducted in four fields. Three  of them were located at the Desmaisieres  farms: 1) wet seeding and continuous flooding (Control); 2) 14% reduction in water inflow/outflow during whole crop cycle and  22% reduction in water inflow/outflow from day 100 after sowing (RT2); 3) longer drying periods and 30% reduction in water inflow/outflow (LDP-RT3); while the last one was located at the Rubiales Farm (and 5) surface drip irrigation (DRIP).\nThe dataset also includes the experimental layouts of the pilot fields and the rice varieties cultivated under each irrigation treatment."
                                                                                                                                           }
                                                                                                                }
                                                                                                            ]
